1. Automatic Evaluation Metrics (AEMs)

Automatic Evaluation Metrics (AEMs) are mainly used to compare the quality of machine-generated text with reference human-written text. These metrics are designed to handle large datasets and can be used to quantify the overall quality of text generated by a LLM. Some popular AEMs used for multilingual tasks are:

  a. BLEU (Bilingual Evaluation Understudy) Score: BLEU scores measure the overlap between machine-generated text and human-written references in terms of n-gram precision (1-gram, 2-gram, 3-gram, etc.). Higher BLEU scores imply a higher degree of similarity between machine-generated and reference humans-written text.

