  c. METEOR (Metric for evaluation of translation with exact precisIon and recall) Score: METEOR scores combine the precision and recall of n-grams, phrase matches, and synonyms to provide a more comprehensive evaluation of the quality of machine-generated text. METEOR scores are normalized between 0 and 1, with higher scores indicating better quality.

  d. TER (Bilingual Evaluation Understudy for Translation Error Reduction) Score: TER scores measure the editing operations (insertions, deletions, substitutions, and translations) required to modify machine-generated text so that it matches human-written references. Lower TER scores indicate better translation quality.

AEMs have been widely used in various assessments of LLMs due to their ability to handle large datasets and automate evaluation. However, they have criticisms related to their reliance on reference texts and inability to capture nuances such as idiomatic expressions, humor, and cultural variations.

