3. Hybrid Evaluation

Hybrid evaluation approaches combine the strengths of both automatic and human assessments. For example, an LLM's generated text can be first evaluated using AEMs to quickly identify promising candidates, and then these candidates can be evaluated by human annotators to provide more nuanced assessments.

4. Limitations and Future Directions

