 How do you design and train a quantized model? This post will explain, demonstrate, and share resources for ML engineers ready to dive into the world of quantization.

If you've ever tried to optimize a deep learning model for deployment on a device with limited memory or compute power, you've probably encountered the concept of model quantization.

Quantization is a technique that reduces the precision of the computations performed by a machine learning model. Models that operate with fewer bits of precision generally have smaller memory footprints and run faster, although this comes at the cost of a decrease in model performance. To put it another way, quantization allows you to make a trade-off between model accuracy and device efficiency while keeping your model size in check.

In this post, I will:

1. Explain what a quantized model is,
2. Describe how to serve quantized models in TensorFlow and PyTorch,
